---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Converter from '../components/Converter.astro';

const title = 'How to Convert KG to LBS - Complete Guide with Formula & Examples';
const description = 'Learn how to convert kilograms to pounds with our step-by-step guide. Includes the kg to lbs formula, worked examples, and a free online converter.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="https://kgtolbs.cc/how-to-convert-kg-to-lbs">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={`{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "HowTo",
    "name": "How to Convert Kilograms to Pounds",
    "description": "${description}",
    "step": [
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "position": 1,
        "name": "Understand the Formula",
        "text": "The formula to convert kg to lbs is: Pounds = Kilograms × 2.20462262185."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "position": 2,
        "name": "Multiply Your KG Value",
        "text": "Take your weight in kilograms and multiply it by 2.2046."
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "position": 3,
        "name": "Get Your Result in LBS",
        "text": "The result is your weight in pounds. For best accuracy, use 2.20462262185 as the multiplier."
      }
    ]
  }`} />

  <div class="container">
    <div class="content-section">
      <h1>How to Convert KG to LBS</h1>
      <p>A complete guide to converting kilograms to pounds, with formulas, examples, and a free converter tool.</p>
    </div>

    <Converter />

    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>The KG to LBS Formula</h2>
      <p>The standard formula is:</p>
      <div class="formula">
        <strong>Pounds (lbs) = Kilograms (kg) × 2.20462262185</strong>
      </div>

      <p>For quick mental math, you can use the approximation:</p>
      <div class="formula">
        Pounds (lbs) &asymp; Kilograms (kg) × 2.2
      </div>

      <h3>Why 2.2046?</h3>
      <p>The international avoirdupois pound is defined as exactly 0.45359237 kilograms. Therefore, 1 kg = 1 / 0.45359237 = 2.20462262185 lbs.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>Worked Examples</h2>

      <h3>Example 1: Convert 75 kg to lbs</h3>
      <div class="formula">75 kg × 2.2046 = { (75 * 2.20462262185).toFixed(2) } lbs</div>

      <h3>Example 2: Convert 62.5 kg to lbs</h3>
      <div class="formula">62.5 kg × 2.2046 = { (62.5 * 2.20462262185).toFixed(2) } lbs</div>

      <h3>Example 3: Convert 100 kg to lbs</h3>
      <div class="formula">100 kg × 2.2046 = { (100 * 2.20462262185).toFixed(2) } lbs</div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>When Do You Need KG to LBS Conversion?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Fitness & Body Weight:</strong> Most countries use kg, but the US and UK often use lbs for body weight.</li>
        <li><strong>Cooking & Baking:</strong> International recipes may list ingredients in kg, while US recipes use lbs.</li>
        <li><strong>Shipping & Logistics:</strong> International shipping weight limits are often specified in both kg and lbs.</li>
        <li><strong>Medical & Healthcare:</strong> Patient weight, medication dosing by weight.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p style="text-align: center; margin: 2rem 0;">
      <a href="/">Start Converting</a> &middot;
      <a href="/conversion-table">View Full Table</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
